Q2. @PathVariable, @RequestParam, @RequestBody
Ans:
What it does
Extracts values from the URL path itself.
- Used when the value is part of the endpoint URI
- Very common in RESTful APIs
- When identifying a specific resource


Example URL
GET /users/101

Controller Code:
@RestController
public class UserController {
    @GetMapping("/users/{id}")
    public User getUser(@PathVariable int id) {
        return new User(id, "Vijay");
    }
}


Multiple Path Variables
@GetMapping("/users/{id}/orders/{orderId}")
public String getOrder(
        @PathVariable int id,
        @PathVariable int orderId) {
    return "User " + id + ", Order " + orderId;
}

Optional PathVariable
@GetMapping({"/users", "/users/{id}"})
public String getUser(@PathVariable(required = false) Integer id) {
    return (id == null) ? "All users" : "User " + id;
}


2. @RequestParam
What it does
Extracts values from query parameters in the URL.
- Used for filters, pagination, sorting, optional data
- Used When passing optional or filtering data


Example URL
GET /users?role=admin&page=2

Controller Code
@GetMapping("/users")
public String getUsers(
        @RequestParam String role,
        @RequestParam int page) {
    return "Role: " + role + ", Page: " + page;
}

Optional Request Parameter
@GetMapping("/users")
public String getUsers(
        @RequestParam(required = false) String role) {
    return role == null ? "All users" : role;
}

With Default Value
@GetMapping("/users")
public String getUsers(
        @RequestParam(defaultValue = "1") int page) {
    return "Page: " + page;
}


3. @RequestBody
What it does
Maps the HTTP request body to a Java object.
- Used mostly with POST, PUT, PATCH
- Converts JSON/XML → Java object using Jackson
- When sending complex data


Example Request
POST /users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "Vijay",
  "email": "vijay@test.com"
}

Controller Code:
@PostMapping("/users")
public User createUser(@RequestBody User user) {
    return user;
}

Validation with @valid
@PostMapping("/users")
public User createUser(@Valid @RequestBody User user) {
    return user;
}



4. Key Differences (Interview Table)

Annotation Data Source Typical HTTP Method Use Case

@PathVariable:  URL path GET, PUT, DELETE Resource identification
@RequestParam: Query parameters / form GET,POST Filters, pagination
@RequestBody: Request body (JSON/XML) POST, PUT, PATCH Create/update resources
