Q4. ResponseEntity 
Ans: 
- It is a Spring Framework (Spring MVC / Spring Boot) class used to represent the entire HTTP response—not just the response body, 
	but also status code and headers.
- It gives you full control over what your REST API returns to the client.

package: org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity

 What ResponseEntity Contains
- A ResponseEntity<T> can include:
- Response body (T)
- HTTP status code (200, 201, 400, 404, etc.)
- HTTP headers (Content-Type, Location, custom headers, etc.)

If you return only an object Spring:
	- Automatically serializes the object
	- Always sends 200 OK
	- You cannot control headers or status

With ResponseEntity, you can.
	@GetMapping("/user")
	public ResponseEntity<User> getUser() {
    		User user = new User("Vijay");
    		return new ResponseEntity<>(user, HttpStatus.OK);
	}
